  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A harness of straps and brass around a mainspring the size of a fist. It ticks in time with its wearer's pulse, and it goes on ticking for an hour after it is taken off.</p><p><strong>Overwind.</strong> Once per day, at the end of your turn, you can take another turn at once. The harness regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>Quicken.</strong> Once per day, as a Bonus Action, you cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplHaste00000]{Haste} on yourself without Concentration, and you are not left sluggish when it ends. The harness regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>Borrowed Time.</strong> Wound backward, the harness lets its wearer live one minute over again: the last minute, once, with everything put back as it was and only the wearer remembering. The mainspring then needs a year and a day to settle before it can be wound that way again.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
